      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T10:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have 29 Vuex modules today. This migration will take a long time, so most of the project will live in a \"half Vuex, half Vue Query\" state for a while. The design doesn\u0027t explain how that period works safely.\n\nMain question: if the same resource (same @odata.id) is cached in both Vuex and Vue Query, which one is correct, and who updates the other when a value changes? Since SSE invalidation is deferred, there\u0027s no answer today.\n\nPlease add a short \"Coexistence\" section with 3 simple rules:\n\nA resource lives in only ONE store at a time.\nMigrate a whole feature at once (view + its child components + delete the store), not half.\nNever cache the same @odata.id in both Vuex and Vue Query.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "70b4007d7c8fe3a044a066b293540f171d8c39fa",
